CHANGE ANALYSIS (citations verified, indeterminate)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────
Cannot be established from this repository alone: the diff and surrounding context alone are not enough to say.
The mechanisms are explicit, but actual user-visible impact requires the new service worker to be built, registered, activated, and controlling a page that issues matching asset requests. Those reachability and runtime facts are not established by the supplied diff.

The web client adds a service worker that intercepts image asset GETs, serves successful responses from a versioned browser cache, supports background preloading, and can abort in-flight image loads when viewers or thumbnails are destroyed. Production tooling also gains a command to stop the production Compose stack. Several end-to-end assertions were removed or relaxed, but the supplied post-change source does not establish a corresponding product behavior change.

Likely behavioral changes
  • Once the service worker controls a page, matching original and thumbnail asset GETs can be returned from a deployment-versioned browser cache; cache misses are fetched and successful 200 responses are stored for later requests.
  • Photo-viewer lookahead loading is now requested through a BroadcastChannel instead of creating an Image object directly, allowing the service worker to fetch and cache the requested image in the background.
  • When a photo loader is cleaned up or a thumbnail action is destroyed, the client asks the service worker to abort a currently tracked fetch for that URL.
  • Operators can now stop the production Docker Compose stack, including orphaned containers, through the new prod-down Make target.

Investigate
  • Trace how the framework builds, registers, updates, and activates this service worker, including whether it immediately controls existing tabs after skipWaiting and clients.claim.
  • Trace all producers and consumers of the immich BroadcastChannel protocol and determine whether URL cancellation is scoped to one component or shared among concurrent consumers and tabs.
  • Inspect the asset endpoint's authorization, request-header, range-request, and caching semantics because interception replaces the original Request with a fetch made from its URL and may serve a cached response without contacting the endpoint.
  • Check test coverage for loading indicators and download progress after the photo-viewer spinner test and shared-link DOWNLOADING assertion were removed.

Uncertain
  • The supplied context does not establish whether the SvelteKit build automatically discovers and registers this service-worker entry, or which supported browsers provide the required BroadcastChannel behavior.
  • The matching URL pattern is visible, but the backend handler and authorization policy serving /api/assets/{id}/original and /api/assets/{id}/thumbnail are not supplied.
  • Whether real pages are controlled by the new worker and issue matching asset requests depends on service-worker activation, browser state, and request URLs at runtime.
  • Whether URL-global cancellation actually conflicts depends on concurrent requests for the same URL and the order in which components are destroyed.
  • The observable effect of cache hits, old-cache deletion, and possible cross-session reuse depends on Cache Storage contents and authentication/account transitions in the browser.

